Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"WqcYEk8bGpAi-fKtH-kAoQ","review_id":"jJC8h3Fsk__AFXYFgJDrxw","date":"2015-10-08T15:41:32","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9304695129394531,"text_excerpt":"My husband and I came here for dinner on a Saturday night with another couple, so we got to try more menu items. I always hate that I cannot remember the names of all items I ordered. The ambiance was great - a little noisy, but we sat near the kitchen on a Saturday night. We didn't get to try any oysters (definitely a must for us next time) but I did get a peek at their sweet oyster bar/area on the way to the bathroom. I had a pink drink with a candied flower called the Damn Thistle, but it was so delicious I had three or four. There was quite a bit of ice in the drink, so I asked them to cut down on that a bit, and that made the drink even better. Everything was great - for apps we got ..."},{"business_id":"WqcYEk8bGpAi-fKtH-kAoQ","review_id":"u4pT7liDv6sJdsmW0Hkn8A","date":"2016-07-24T22:34:52","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9278658628463745,"text_excerpt":"Sac-A-Lait has to be one of my top 5 restaurants in the city right now. I've been here a couple of times for dinner and my first time for happy hour just a couple days ago. Be sure to sit at the bar to participate in Happy Hour, otherwise, it's regular price if you dine at the tables. What to Order: 1. Happy Hour oysters! So good. I do miss the regular saltine crackers but the Sac-a-Lait crisp does the job. 2.The Pig's Ear was a tease since you literally get one ear (as gross as this sounds to some people). That first bite has a crunchy crisp with a deliciously chewy and juicy bite. It paired very well with the accompanied cream sauce topped with black sea caviar. I wish I had a bagful of..."},{"business_id":"WqcYEk8bGpAi-fKtH-kAoQ","review_id":"ZZ4VlfQSK_g4lqimlkr52w","date":"2017-10-29T22:01:43","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9274252653121948,"text_excerpt":"This is my second time here, and again it did not disappoint. We walked in which is unusual for a NOLA restaurant but we were lucky. Our waiter, Maurice was very knowledgeable and exceptionally attentive which is rare nowadays. We had great cocktails- their house mixed/barreled bourbon was excellent. Until t'amaro and damn thistle were tasty. We shared several dishes, including a dozen of the visiting raw oysters (small and salty the way we love them), the crab bisque, back strap, gator/mirliton dish, and duck hearts. It was great. Highly recommend for a very unusual menu."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"WqcYEk8bGpAi-fKtH-kAoQ","photo_id":"eKJg44rsWqlHKzBG25fJPg","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/eKJg44rsWqlHKzBG25fJPg.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8615704774856567},{"business_id":"WqcYEk8bGpAi-fKtH-kAoQ","photo_id":"vV_wcJnpZWbrwpC6jNEwGw","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/vV_wcJnpZWbrwpC6jNEwGw.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8607363104820251},{"business_id":"WqcYEk8bGpAi-fKtH-kAoQ","photo_id":"_uo5sPJv0fV7hBIyYavD5Q","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/_uo5sPJv0fV7hBIyYavD5Q.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8538978099822998},{"business_id":"WqcYEk8bGpAi-fKtH-kAoQ","photo_id":"MTmGOIP-0JUr5Q98GWQ6ag","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/MTmGOIP-0JUr5Q98GWQ6ag.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8514389991760254},{"business_id":"Wq